    <name>
      <text>Double Intergrals_Question 5</text>
    </name>
    <questiontext format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p>Compute double integral over the indicated rectangle.</p>
<p>\( \displaystyle \int \int_R {@question_expr@} dA \quad R=[{@lower_x@},{@upper_x@} ] \times [{@lower_y@},{@upper_y@}]\)</p><br>
<p><b>Hint:</b> Rewrite the integral as follows, </p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \int \int_R {@question_expr@} dA = \int_{@lower_x@}^{@upper_x@} \int_{@lower_y@}^{@upper_y@}{@question_expr@} dydx \)</p><br>
<p><b>Step1:</b> Compute the definite integral of the function with respect to \(y\). Assume that the \(x\) is a constant.</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \int_{@lower_y@}^{@upper_y@}{@question_expr@} dy=\)[[input:ans1]] [[validation:ans1]][[feedback:prt1]]</p><br>
<p><b>Step2:</b>Integrate your input answer in <b>Step 1</b> above with respect to \(x\). Such that, <b>(Write your answer in 2 decimal places)</b></p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \int_{@lower_x@}^{@upper_x@} \int_{@lower_y@}^{@upper_y@}{@question_expr@} dydx= \) [[input:ans2]] [[validation:ans2]][[feedback:prt2]]</p>]]></text>
    </questiontext>
    <generalfeedback format="moodle_auto_format">
      <text><![CDATA[<p><b>Worked Solution</b></p>
<p><b>Step1:</b> In order to integrate the function with respect to \(y\), we need to use \(u\)-substitution.</p>
<p>\(\displaystyle \int_{@lower_y@}^{@upper_y@}{@question_expr@} dy\)</p>
<p>Let \(u={@let_u@} \rightarrow {@diff_u@}\) and \({@var_y@}\)</p>
<p>Now let us substitute the above in the original equation. </p>
<p>\(
\begin{align}
\displaystyle \int_{@lower_y@}^{@upper_y@}{@question_expr@} dy &=\int_{@lower_y@}^{@upper_y@}{@rhs(var_y)@}{@%e^u@} dy \\
  &=\int_{@lower_y@}^{@upper_y@} {@expr1@} \\
  &={@1/2@} \int_{@lower_y@}^{@upper_y@} e^{u}du \\
 &={@1/2@}  \left(e^{u}\right) \left.\begin{matrix}& \\ & \end{matrix}\right|_{@lower_y@}^{@upper_y@} \\
 &={@1/2@}  \left(e^{{@power_e@}}\right) \left.\begin{matrix}& \\ & \end{matrix}\right|_{@lower_y@}^{@upper_y@} \\
&={@ta1@}  
\end{align}
\)</p>
<p><b>Step 2:</b> The next step is to repeat <b>step 1</b>, but integrate wrt to \(x\),</p>
<p>\(
\begin{align}
\displaystyle \int \int_R {@question_expr@} dA &=\int_{@lower_x@}^{@upper_x@} {@ta1@} dx \\
 &= \left({@int_xx@}\right) \left.\begin{matrix}& \\ & \end{matrix}\right|_{@lower_x@}^{@upper_x@} \\
&={@int_x@} \\
&={@ta2@}  
\end{align}
\)</p>]]></text>
    </generalfeedback>
